Future Goals
The project is structured with goals to guide ongoing development:
1. Interactive Calendar – completed; allows creation/editing of shifts with drag, resize, and modal.
2. Notifications and Reminders – implement email or SMS notifications when schedules are created or modified.
3. Advanced Metrics – expand the analytics dashboard with indicators of absenteeism, seasonality, and cost comparison.
4. Skills Module – associate certifications/competencies with employees to direct schedules based on business needs.
5. Progressive Web App (PWA) – enable installation on mobile devices and basic offline use.
6. Optimization and Forecasting Algorithms – integrate machine learning or linear programming models to predict demand and optimize schedules.
Contribution and Customization
· To customize appearance, adjust style files (CSS) or replace Bootstrap theme. Icons and animations can be added with Font Awesome or Animate.css.
· To integrate AI modules, it is recommended to create microservices in Python (e.g., using Flask) exposing REST APIs; PHP consumes these services and displays results in the interface.
· Migrating the database from SQLite to MySQL or PostgreSQL is possible by changing the connection string in config.php and adjusting SQL syntax as needed.
